{% set opposite = {"outer":"inner", "inner":"outer"} %}
{% set other_placement = opposite[param_placement] %}
links:
  # The bracket is the fixture: everything else is connected to it, so it is
  # placed rather than connected and is held by its own foot.
  - part: example-bracket

  - part: example-motor
    connect:
      with: nema-17-motor-mount
      name: example-bracket
      to: nema-17-motor-bracket-3
      toInstance: {{ param_placement }}
      toPort: "*TR*"
      comment: |
        The motor is heavy enough to fall out of an unclamped bracket, so seat
        it before any of the screws go in. It is only pushed into place here -
        the thread the two M3 hole patterns share is cut by the screws below,
        not by this step.
      how:
        stage: seat-the-motor
        # A straight push: "turnTorqueMax" stays at its default of zero.
        pushForceMax: 30.0
        holdWith: nema-17-motor-mount
        holdWithForceMin: 8.0
        holdWithForceMax: 20.0
        holdTo: nema-17-motor-bracket-3
        holdToInstance: {{ param_placement }}

  {% for corner in ['TL', 'BR', 'TR', 'BL'] %}
  - part: socket-head-m3-screw-6mm
    name: m3-{{ corner }}
    connect:
      name: example-bracket
      to: m3-thru-3
      toInstance: {{ other_placement }}-{{ corner }}
      {% if corner == 'TL' %}
      comment: |
        The four M3 screws go in diagonally opposite pairs and in two passes:
        every one of them is started before any of them is tightened, so that
        the motor stays square to the bracket. "threadStep" is not given here -
        it is inherited from the M3 interfaces, which carry the 0.5mm pitch.
      {% endif %}
      how:
        stage: m3-snug
        turnDirection: cw
        turnTorqueMax: 0.4
  {% endfor %}

  {% for side in ['R', 'L'] %}
  - part: socket-head-m4-screw-6mm
    name: m4-{{ side }}
    connect:
      with: m4-screw-6mm
      name: example-bracket
      to: m4-slotted-30-thru-3
      toInstance: {{ side }}
      toParams: { offset: -15 }
      {% if side == 'R' %}
      comment: |
        The foot screws are last: the slots let the bracket slide, so they are
        left loose until the motor is square, and only then torqued down.
      {% endif %}
      how:
        stage: m4-final
        turnDirection: cw
        turnTorqueMax: 1.7
        # The bracket is held by the other slot while this one is driven.
        holdTo: m4-slotted-30-thru-3
        holdToInstance: {{ 'L' if side == 'R' else 'R' }}
  {% endfor %}
